---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ComparisonBars from '../components/ComparisonBars.astro';
import CriterionLegend from '../components/CriterionLegend.astro';
import { loadPublication, basePath } from '../lib/data.js';
import type { Publication } from '../lib/domain';
import { DISPLAY_INDEX, criterionAbbreviation } from '../lib/criteria';
import { TIER_LABELS } from '../lib/labels';
import { eipRoute } from '../lib/routes';
import { signed } from '../lib/format';

const data = loadPublication() as Publication;
const alignment = data.human_llm;
const summary = alignment.summary;
const definitions = new Map(data.criteria.map((item) => [item.id, item]));
const hegota = data.forks.find((item) => item.fork === 'hegota');
const hegotaHuman = hegota.human_coverage;
const criteria = [...alignment.criteria].sort((a, b) => Math.abs(b.mean_delta) - Math.abs(a.mean_delta) || (DISPLAY_INDEX.get(a.id) ?? 99) - (DISPLAY_INDEX.get(b.id) ?? 99));
const only3 = data.criteria.filter((item) => item.rubric_revisions.includes(3) && !item.rubric_revisions.includes(1)).map((item) => item.id);
const newCriterionPoints = alignment.rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + data.assessments[row.llm_assessment_id].criteria.filter((item) => only3.includes(item.id)).reduce((part, item) => part + (item.score ?? 0), 0), 0);
const format = (value: number) => (Math.abs(value) < 0.005 ? '0' : (value > 0 ? '+' : '−') + Math.abs(value).toFixed(2));
---
<Layout title="Human versus LLM evaluations" description="Descriptive comparison of published STEEL human complexity checklists with the study's Opus 5.5 · checklist revision 3 assessments for Amsterdam, per EIP and per criterion, and the status of human checklists for Hegotá candidates.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Amsterdam Comparison</p><h1>Human and LLM Complexity Evaluations</h1>
  <p class="lede">A descriptive comparison of published human assessments with the study’s LLM assessments (Claude Opus 5.5, checklist revision 3) for 12 Amsterdam Execution Layer EIPs.</p>
  <div class="source-note"><strong>Why Amsterdam?</strong> It is currently the only fork with a completed human complexity evaluation; the separate manual evaluation for Hegotá is still underway (<a href={basePath('prospective/hegota/')}>{hegotaHuman.scored_count} of {hegota.eip_count} Hegotá candidates</a> have a scored human checklist, and each Hegotá EIP page shows its Human status and a comparison where a scored checklist exists). This page compares the Amsterdam LLM-based and human assessments to examine how closely they align and whether their disagreements reflect systematic differences in how the complexity criteria were interpreted. It is a structured sanity check, not evidence that the LLM is calibrated to human judgment.</div>
  <div class="notice"><strong>Different checklist revisions, same substance.</strong> The human reviewers used <a href="https://github.com/ethspecs/pm/blob/d936bcb34963cb5eec015dada2e4188e49fc14d5/Templates/EIP-Complexity-Assessment.md">checklist revision 1</a> (24 criteria); the LLM used <a href="https://github.com/ethspecs/pm/blob/fe2f793b031adbb17826cfebd5bd2b502d1885c1/Templates/EIP-Complexity-Assessment.md">revision 3</a> (28 criteria), which phrases the same criteria more precisely. Per-criterion differences cover the {alignment.shared_criteria} criteria both revisions share. Totals are compared as published, so the LLM total also includes five criteria revision 1 does not have: {(newCriterionPoints / alignment.rows.length).toFixed(1)} points per EIP on average here. Both evaluated the same historical EIP revision.</div>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><span class="muted">EIPs compared</span><div class="stat">{summary.comparison_count}</div><span class="muted">{alignment.shared_criteria} shared criteria per EIP</span></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="muted">Mean Δ total (LLM − Human)</span><div class="stat">{format(summary.mean_signed_delta)}</div><span class="muted">mean |Δ| {summary.mean_absolute_delta.toFixed(2)} · median |Δ| {summary.median_absolute_delta}</span></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="muted">Who scored higher</span><div class="stat">{summary.llm_higher_count} <span class="stat-unit">LLM</span> · {summary.human_higher_count} <span class="stat-unit">Human</span></div><span class="muted">{summary.equal_total_count} equal totals</span></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="muted">Same tier</span><div class="stat">{summary.tier_agreement_count} <span class="stat-unit">of {summary.comparison_count}</span></div><span class="muted">each evaluator’s own tier thresholds (revision 1: &lt;10 · 10–19 · ≥20; revision 3: &lt;12 · 12–22 · ≥23)</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="per-eip">Complexity profiles per EIP</h2>
  <p class="muted">Human (revision 1) and LLM (revision 3) profiles for each EIP on one shared scale, ranked by the Human total. Δ is LLM minus Human. Open an EIP for its per-criterion comparison with the rationale from both evaluators.</p>
  <ComparisonBars data={data} rows={alignment.rows} fork="amsterdam" />

  <h2 id="per-criterion">Where the Evaluators Differ by Criterion</h2>
  <p class="muted">Mean per-criterion difference across the 12 EIPs, LLM minus Human, for the {alignment.shared_criteria} criteria both revisions share. Positive values mean the LLM scored the criterion higher on average.</p>
  <div class="table-region" role="region" aria-label="Per-criterion Human versus LLM differences" tabindex="0">
    <table class="criterion-table criterion-aggregate" data-sortable-table>
      <caption>Per-criterion differences across 12 Amsterdam EIPs (shared criteria of revisions 1 and 3)</caption>
      <thead><tr>
        <th scope="col" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortCriterion">Criterion</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortMean" data-sort-kind="number">Mean Δ</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortAbs" data-sort-kind="number">Mean |Δ|</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortLlmHigher" data-sort-kind="number">LLM higher</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortHumanHigher" data-sort-kind="number">Human higher</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortExact" data-sort-kind="number">Agree</button></th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {criteria.map((row) => (
          <tr class:list={[Math.abs(row.mean_delta) >= 0.5 && 'aggregate-notable']} data-sort-criterion={String(DISPLAY_INDEX.get(row.id) ?? 99).padStart(2, '0')} data-sort-mean={row.mean_delta} data-sort-abs={row.mean_absolute_delta} data-sort-llm-higher={row.llm_higher_count} data-sort-human-higher={row.human_higher_count} data-sort-exact={row.exact_count}>
            <th scope="row"><span class="swatch" style={`--fill:var(--criterion-${row.id});--ink:var(--criterion-ink-${row.id})`} aria-hidden="true">{criterionAbbreviation(row.id)}</span><span class="criterion-name">{definitions.get(row.id).label}</span></th>
            <td class:list={['number', 'delta', row.mean_delta > 0 && 'delta-pos', row.mean_delta < 0 && 'delta-neg']}>{format(row.mean_delta)}</td>
            <td class="number">{row.mean_absolute_delta.toFixed(2)}</td>
            <td class="number">{row.llm_higher_count}</td>
            <td class="number">{row.human_higher_count}</td>
            <td class="number">{row.exact_count}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="totals">Totals per EIP</h2>
  <div class="table-region" role="region" aria-label="Human and LLM complexity totals" tabindex="0">
    <table data-sortable-table>
      <caption>Amsterdam totals per EIP: Human (checklist revision 1) and LLM (Opus 5.5, checklist revision 3)</caption>
      <thead><tr>
        <th scope="col" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortEip" data-sort-kind="number">EIP</button></th>
        <th scope="col" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortTitle">Proposal</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortHuman" data-sort-kind="number">Human r1</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortLlm" data-sort-kind="number">LLM r3</button></th>
        <th scope="col" class="number" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortDelta" data-sort-kind="number">Δ</button></th>
        <th scope="col" aria-sort="none"><button class="sort-button" type="button" data-sort-key="sortTier">Tiers</button></th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>{alignment.rows.map((row) => <tr data-human-llm-eip={row.eip} data-sort-eip={row.eip} data-sort-title={row.title} data-sort-human={row.human_total} data-sort-llm={row.llm_total} data-sort-delta={row.delta} data-sort-tier={row.tier_agreement ? '0' : '1'}><td><a href={eipRoute(row.eip, { fork: 'amsterdam', view: 'compare' })}>EIP-{row.eip}</a></td><td>{row.title}</td><td class="number">{row.human_total}</td><td class="number">{row.llm_total}</td><td class:list={['number', 'delta', row.delta > 0 && 'delta-pos', row.delta < 0 && 'delta-neg']}>{signed(row.delta)}</td><td>{row.tier_agreement ? <span class:list={['pill', 'pill-small', row.human_tier]}>{TIER_LABELS[row.human_tier]}</span> : <><span class:list={['pill', 'pill-small', row.human_tier]}>{TIER_LABELS[row.human_tier]}</span> <span class="muted">vs</span> <span class:list={['pill', 'pill-small', row.llm_tier]}>{TIER_LABELS[row.llm_tier]}</span></>}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What Differed Systematically?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The LLM scored higher overall.</strong> Its total exceeded the human total for {summary.llm_higher_count} of {summary.comparison_count} EIPs, by {format(summary.mean_signed_delta)} points on average. About {(newCriterionPoints / alignment.rows.length).toFixed(1)} points per EIP come from the five criteria that revision 1 does not have.</li>
    <li><strong>Cross-EIP interactions and security drove the shared-criterion excess.</strong> The LLM scored Cross-EIP interactions higher for 11 of 12 EIPs and Security risks higher for 9.</li>
    <li><strong>Humans scored EVM gas rules higher.</strong> The human checklists scored more gas-accounting work on five EIPs; the LLM never exceeded them on that criterion.</li>
    <li><strong>Tiers agreed for {summary.tier_agreement_count} of {summary.comparison_count} EIPs</strong>, each against its own revision’s thresholds; most disagreements are human Low against LLM Medium.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are descriptive differences across 12 EIPs. The comparison crosses checklist revisions and evaluation times, so it neither validates nor calibrates either evaluator.</p>
  <CriterionLegend criteria={data.criteria} revision={3} compact={true} summary="Criterion legend for the revision-3 checklist" />
  <div class="actions"><a href={basePath('generated/downloads/criterion-scores.csv')}>Download criterion scores (CSV)</a><a href={basePath('eips/compare/?a=amsterdam:7928:llm:r3,amsterdam:7928:human:r1')}>Open a Human vs LLM pair in the comparison view</a><a href={basePath()}>Read the methodology and limitations</a></div>
</Layout>
